@startuml Create Banner Sequence Diagram
title UC-BN03 - Create Banner

actor "Admin" as User
participant "Banner\nGovernance Page" as Frontend
participant ":bannerRoutes" as Routes
participant ":bannerController" as Controller
participant ":bannerService" as Service
participant "Canteen\nModel" as CanteenModel
participant "Banner\nModel" as BannerModel
database "MongoDB" as DB

User -> Frontend: 1. Click "Create Banner"\nEnter title, imageUrl, linkUrl, order...
Frontend -> Frontend: 2. Validate required fields
Frontend -> Routes: 3. POST /api/banners (Bearer Token, bannerData)

ref over Routes
Verify JWT Token and Admin Role
end ref
Routes -> Routes: 4. Check authentication/authorization result
opt [Unauthorized]
  Routes --> Frontend: 5. 401/403 error
  Frontend --> User: 6. Show error
end

Routes -> Controller: 7. createBanner(req, res)
Controller -> Service: 8. createBanner(data, userId)
Service -> Service: 9. Validate payload (date, canteenId)

Service -> Service: 9.1 Check validation result
opt [Invalid payload]
  Service --> Controller: 9.2 Throw AppError(400)
  Controller --> Routes: 9.3 JSON error
  Routes --> Frontend: 9.4 JSON error response
  Frontend --> User: 9.5 Show error
end

Service -> CanteenModel: 10. findById(canteenId) (if provided)
CanteenModel -> DB: 11. Check canteen existence
DB --> CanteenModel: 12. Result

Service -> BannerModel: 13. create({ ...data, createdBy: userId })
BannerModel -> DB: 14. Insert banner
DB --> BannerModel: 15. New banner
BannerModel --> Service: 16. Banner object

Service --> Controller: 17. Return banner
Controller --> Routes: 18. HTTP 201
Routes --> Frontend: 19. JSON response { banner }
Frontend --> User: 20. Show "Banner created successfully"

@enduml
